From 45f76c5052c17dab800602f74d1d2c256246a3ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:03:25 +0200
Subject: glm: TF_GLM_PF_DOWN_FUSE, the routed down sums the route slots (fused
 combine)

TF_GLM_PF_DOWN_FUSE=1 (default off): in the two-halves prompt path (TF_GLM_DSA_HALVES with
TF_GLM_HALVES_EXPERTS_WHOLE, EXL3 experts on bf16 slot rows) the routed down kernel
(tf_exl3_prompt_down_fuse / _k6_fuse) counts each pair's written 256-column slice in
cnt[row][cb]; the warp that completes a row's 8 routed pairs sums them as tf_glm_combine does
(fp32 fma from +0 over the slots in order, bf16 slot value x wts[row][slot]) and, for the first
half's rows, the shared expert's slot (put_slot's bf16 rounding, weight wts[row][8]), and writes
the half's exchange rows directly. The second half's shared slot follows its shared expert as
tf_glm_fold_slot (the combine's last fma). No put_slot, no slot-row combine. Integer counters and
a fixed summation order: the same bits as down + put_slot + combine.

The launch is 1-D in bands of column blocks (TF_GLM_PF_DOWN_FUSE_BAND, default 12 of 24; launch
order only) and drops the read partial lines from the L2 (discard.global.L2).

Exactness (spark6, harness on the built fatbins vs down_b16 + put_slot + combine): bitwise equal
on GLM-5.3 EXL3 K4 layers 10 and 40 (rank-0 TP4 down pieces) and random K4/K3 weights, rows
2048-4096, splits 0 / half / all, bands 1-24, discard on/off; four mutations (slot order, mul+add,
early last arriver, unrounded shared slot) fail. Existing kernels' SASS unchanged.
Microbench per layer (4,096 rows): 4.93 + 3.20 = 8.13 ms -> 6.58 + 0.63 = 7.21 ms.

The fused combine follows the design of kindlingai/gr8's expert-tile fc2 (GR8_PF_WT_FUSE and
GR8_PF_WT_GMAJOR, MIT) by Matt Mastracci: a warp that completes a token's routes sums them in
route order, group-major launch so the partials stay in the L2. This code is written fresh for
TensorFold's kernels.

